<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SharedKernelTier>Host</SharedKernelTier>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>MediatR as the transport behind SharedKernel.Application's ISender. AddSharedKernelMediatR(assemblies) scans for the kernel's own handler types — IRequestHandler (ICommandHandler/IQueryHandler), IStreamQueryHandler and IDomainEventHandler — and registers, for each request type, a MediatR handler that runs the kernel's RequestPipeline: the behaviors registered by SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline, then the handler.

This is the only SharedKernel package that references MediatR. Commands, queries, handlers and behaviors are written against SharedKernel.Application, so replacing MediatR is a different implementation of ISender and changes no application code. Pinned to MediatR 12.4.1, the last MIT-licensed release.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>First release.

WHAT IS IN IT
- AddSharedKernelMediatR(params Assembly[] assemblies): registers MediatR, the kernel ISender, RequestPipeline/StreamRequestPipeline, the native DomainEventDispatcher, and every kernel handler found in the assemblies.

THINGS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU ADOPT IT
- It registers no behaviors: call AddSharedKernelApplicationBehaviors()...Build() (SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline) for those. MediatR's own pipeline stays empty; the kernel pipeline runs inside the MediatR handler.
- A request can be sent only if its handler was found in a scanned assembly. Sending anything else throws InvalidOperationException naming the request type.
- Implement the kernel interfaces, never MediatR's: a class implementing MediatR.IRequestHandler or INotificationHandler is not discovered.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>cqrs;mediatr;mediator;application;shared-kernel</PackageTags>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);nullable;CS1591;RS0016;RS0017;RS0022;RS0024;RS0025;RS0036;RS0037</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SharedKernel.Application\SharedKernel.Application.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline\SharedKernel.Application.Pipeline.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The ONLY project in the repository that references MediatR (locked by
      MediatRReferenceRules in SharedKernel.ArchitectureTests). Pinned to 12.4.x, the last
      MIT-licensed major (v13 introduced a commercial license).
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="MediatR" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Shipped.txt" />
    <AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
